t Pricing.\nL86: ### Select a Size\nL87: \nL88: Change View\nL89: Size/SKU  | Availability  | Price\nL90: --- | --- | ---\nL91: 25 g H3375-25G  | Available to ship TODAY  | $65.20\nL92: 100 g H3375-100G  | Available to ship TODAY  | $121.00\nL93: 250 g H3375-250G  | Available to ship TODAY  | $278.00\nL94: 500 g H3375-500G  | Available to ship TODAY  | $502.00\nL95: 1 kg H3375-1KG  | Available to ship TODAY  | $918.00\nL96: 5 kg H3375-5KG  | Available to ship TODAY from MILWAUKEE  | $3,060.00\nL97: 25 kg H3375-25KG  | Available to ship TODAY  | 【12†Inquire】\nL98: 50 kg H3375-50KG  | Available to ship TODAY  | 【12†Inquire】\nL99: * * *\nL100: ### About This Item\nL101: \nL102: Empirical Formula (Hill Notation):\nL103: \nL104: C_{8}H_{18}N_{2}O_{4}S\nL105: \nL106: CAS Number:\nL107: \nL108: 【13†7365-45-9】\nL109: \nL110: Molecular Weight:\nL111: \nL112: 238.30\nL113: \nL114: UNSPSC Code:\nL115: \nL116: 12161700\nL117: \nL118: NACRES:\nL119: \nL120: NA.25\nL121: \nL122: PubChem Substance ID:\nL123: \nL124: 【14†24895572†pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov】\nL125: \nL126: EC Number:\nL127: \nL128: 230-907-9\nL129: \nL130: Beilstein/REAXYS Number:\nL131: \nL132: 883043\nL133: \nL134: MDL number:\nL135: \nL136: 【15†MFCD00006158】\nL137: \nL138: eCl@ss:\nL139: \nL140: 32160703\nL141: \nL142: ## H3375-25G\nL143: ### $65.20\nL144: \nL145: * * *\nL146: \nL147: Available to ship TODAY Details\nL148: \nL149: * * *\nL150: \nL151: [Input]\nL152: \nL153: One Time Order\nL154: \nL155: ​\nL156: \nL157: [Input]\nL158: \nL159: [Button: Add to Cart]\nL160: \nL161: 【12†Request a Custom Order】\nL162: \nL163: Subscriptions are currently unavailable.\nL164: \nL165: ​\nL166: \nL167: [Input]\nL168: \nL169: Ships Every 4 weeks\nL170: \nL171: [Input]\nL172: \nL173: [Button: Add to Cart]\nL174: \nL175: Technical Service\nL176: \nL177: Need help? Our team of experienced scientists is here for you.\nL178: \nL179: 【16†Let Us Assist】\nL180: \nL181: * * *\nL182: \nL183: * * *\nL184: \nL185: Properties\nL186: \nL187: ### Quality Segment\nL188: \nL189: 【17†400】\nL190: \nL191: ### assay\nL192: \nL193: ≥99.5% (titration)\nL194: \nL195: ### form\nL196: \nL197: crystalline powder\nL198: ### storage condition\nL199: \nL200: dry at room temperature\nL201: \nL202: ### technique(s)\nL203: \nL204: cell culture | mammalian: suitable\nL205: \nL206: ### color\nL207: \nL208: white\nL209: \nL210: ### pH\nL211: \nL212: 5.0-6.5 (25 °C, 238 g/L)\nL213: \nL214: ### useful pH range\nL215: \nL216: 6.8-8.2\nL217: \nL218: ### pKa (25 °C)\nL219: \nL220: 7.5\nL221: \nL222: ### solubility\nL223: \nL224: water: 500 mg/mL, clear, colorless\nL225: \nL226: ### suitability\nL227: \nL228: suitable for component for culture media, suitable for enzyme extraction\nL229: \nL230: ### application(s)\nL231: \nL232: advanced drug delivery\nL233: diagnostic assay manufacturing\nL234: general analytical\nL235: life science and biopharma\nL236: pharmaceutical\nL237: ### SMILES string\nL238: \nL239: OCCN1CCN(CC1)CCS(O)(=O)=O\nL240: \nL241: ### InChI\nL242: \nL243: 1S/C8H18N2O4S/c11-7-5-9-1-3-10(4-2-9)6-8-15(12,13)14/h11H,1-8H2,(H,12,13,14)\nL244: \nL245: ### InChI key\nL246: \nL247: JKMHFZQWWAIEOD-UHFFFAOYSA-N\nL248: \nL249: Description\nL250: ### General description\nL251: HEPES, also known as 4-(2-Hydroxyethyl)piperazine-1-ethane-sulfonic acid, is a zwitterionic N-substituted aminosulfonic acid buffer. It is effective in the pH 6.8-8.2 range, with a pKa of 7.48 at 25°C. Recognized as one of the best all-purpose buffers, especially in cell biology, biochemical, and biological research, HEPES is a dipolar ionic buffer and one of the Good′s buffers that does not form significant complexes with most metal ions.\nL252: This property makes it suitable as a non-coordinating buffer in solutions with metal ions.\nL253: Widely utilized in cell culture, HEPES excels at maintaining physiological pH despite fluctuations in carbon dioxide concentration produced by cellular respiration, a feature not as prominent in bicarbonate buffers. It serves as an ampholytic separator for creating pH gradients in isoelectric focusing and exhibits less interference with DNA-restriction enzyme reactions compared to buffers with fewer substituted amine groups, such as Tris.\nL254: Beyond these applications, HEPES may find application in various biological and biochemical studies, including immunoprecipitation, cell lysis, and live cell imaging. Its versatility makes it an indispensable tool in diverse research applications.\nL255: HEPES has been described as one of the best all-purpose buffers available for biological research. At biological pH, the molecule is zwitterionic, and is effective as a buffer at pH 6.8 to 8.2. HEPES has been used in a wide variety of applications, including tissue culture. It is commonly used to buffer cell culture media in air. HEPES finds its usage in in vitro experiments on Mg.\nL256: ### Application\nL257: \nL258: HEPES has been used:\nL259:   * As a component in Danieau medium, which is used to prevent melanin pigment formation post gastrulation of zebra-fish embryo\nL260:   * As a component of Hanks′ solution used in the degradation testing of Iron\nL261:   * As a component of HEPES medium in the transfection of cell culture with plasmids\nL262:   * Along with RPMI-1640, L-glutamine, FBS, Sodium pyruvate and β-mercaptoethanol for the culturing of rat insulinoma cells\nL263:   * As a supplement in TCM199 medium for washing fresh oocytes required for nuclear transfer studies\nL264: ### Features and Benefits\nL265: \nL266:   * High purity product for biochemical and biological research\nL267:   * Suitable for Cell culture\nL268:   * Highly soluble in water with a useful pH range of 6.8 - 8.2 and pKa of 7.5 at 25 °C\nL269: ### Other Notes\nL270: \nL271: 【18†Go to Redi-Dri^{™} Product Listing RDD002】\nL272: Easily compare specifications for HEPES products with the 【19†HEPES specification table】.\nL273: \nL274: 【20†2024 CiteAb Award Winner for Supplier Succeeding in Parkinson′s Research†www.citeab.com】\nL275: \nL276: For additional information on our range of 【21†Biochemicals】, please complete this 【22†form】.\nL277: \nL278: ### Legal Information\nL279: \nL280: Redi-Dri is a trademark of Sigma-Aldrich Co. LLC\nL281: \nL282: * * *\nL283: ## Compare Similar Items\nL284: \nL285: 【23†View Full Comparison】\nL286: \nL287: * * *\nL288: \nL289: Show Differences\nL290: \nL291: [Input]\nL292: \nL293: 1 of 1\nL294: ###### This Item\nL295:  | RDD002  | PHR1428  | H4034\nL296: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL297: 【24†Sigma-Aldrich H3375 HEPES】[Button: Quick View]  | 【25†Sigma-Aldrich RDD002 HEPES】[Button: Quick View]  | 【26†Supelco PHR1428 HEPES】[Button: Quick View]  | 【27†Sigma-Aldrich H4034 HEPES】[Button: Quick View]\nL298: description≥99.5% (titration)  | description anhydrous, free-flowing, Redi-Dri^{™}, ≥99.5%  | description Pharmaceutical Secondary Standard; Certified Reference Material  | description BioPerformance Certified, ≥99.5% (titration), suitable for cell culture\nL299: assay≥99.5% (titration)  | assay≥99.5%  | assay-  | assay≥99.5% (titration)\nL300: technique(s)cell culture | mammalian: suitable  | technique(s)-  | technique(s)gas chromatography (GC): suitable, HPLC: suitable  | technique(s)cell culture | mammalian: suitable, competitive inhibition ELISA: suitable\nL301: Quality Level 400  | Quality Level 100  | Quality Level 300  | Quality Level 400\nL302: application(s)advanced drug delivery\nL303: diagnostic assay manufacturing\nL304: general analytical\nL305: life science and biopharma\nL306: pharmaceutical  | application(s)-  | application(s)pharmaceutical\nL307: pharmaceutical (small molecule)  | application(s)advanced drug delivery\nL308: clinical research\nL309: diagnostic assay manufacturing\nL310: general analytical\nL311: life science and biopharma\nL312: form crystalline powder  | form crystalline powder  | form-  | form crystalline powder\nL313: solubility water: 500 mg/mL, clear, colorless  | solubility water: 500 mg/mL, clear, colorless  | solubility-  | solubility-\nL314: * * *\nL315: ### Still not finding the right product?\nL316: \nL317: Explore all of our products under 【28†HEPES】\nL318: \nL319: 【28†View All Products】\nL320: \nL321: * * *\nL322: \nL323: ## Safety Information\nL324: \nL325: ### Storage Class\nL326: \nL327: 11 - Combustible Solids\nL328: \nL329: ### Flash Point (°F)\nL330: \nL331: Not applicable\nL332: \nL333: ### Flash Point (°C)\nL334: \nL335: Not applicable\nL336: \nL337: ### PPE (personal protective equipment)\nL338: \nL339: Eyeshields, Gloves, type N95 (US)\nL340: \nL341: * * *\nL342: \nL343: ## Documentation\nL344: \nL345: [Button: Certificate of Analysis][Button: Certificate of Origin]\nL346: \nL347: * * *\nL348: \nL349: Choose from one of the most recent versions:\nL350: ### Certificates of Analysis (COA)\nL351: \nL352: Lot/Batch Number\nL353: \nL354: It looks like we've run into a problem, but you can still download Certificates of Analysis from our 【29†Documents】 section.\nL355: \nL356: If you need assistance, please contact 【16†Customer Support】\nL357: \nL358: ### Already Own This Product?\nL359: \nL360: Find documentation for the products that you have recently purchased in the Document Library.\nL361: \nL362: 【30†Visit the Document Library】\nL363: \nL364: * * *\nL365: ## Product Citations\nL366: \nL367: * * *\nL368: \nL369: * * *\nL370: \nL371: Related Categories\nL372: \nL373: 【5†Biochemicals】\nL374: \nL375: 【31†Biological Buffers】\nL376: \nL377: 【32†HEPES Buffer】\nL378: \nL379: * * *\nL380: \nL381: ★★★★★ ★★★★★ 5 out of 5 stars. Read reviews for HEPES\nL382:     5.0\nL383:     【33†1 Review This action will navigate to reviews.】\nL384: \nL385: Search questions and answers ϙ [Input: Search questions and answers] Search questions and answers ✘ Clear Search field ϙ Search\nL386: \nL387:   * 【33†1 Review】\nL388:   * 【33†7 Questions】\nL389:   * 【33†7 Answers】\nL390: ## Questions\nL391: \nL392: [Button: Ask a question ]\nL393: \nL394: 1–7 of 7 Questions\nL395: \nL396: Sort by: ▼ Menu\nL397: \nL398: [Select]\nL399: \nL400:   1. · 9 months ago\nL401: ### Hello, Is it possible that there are traces of iron or zinc in the final product ? Thank you\nL402: \nL403: 1 answer\nL404: \nL405:     1. Technical Support\nL406: \nL407: · 9 months ago\nL408: Trace metal analysis is not performed on this product. The iron and zinc levels are not determined. However, testing for product 54457, HEPES for molecular biology, BioUltra, does include trace metal analysis, included iron and zinc. Please see the link below to review a sample or lot-specific Certificate of Analysis for the 54457, HEPES.\nL409: 【34†https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sigma/54457#product-documentation】\nL410: \nL411: Helpful?\nL412: \nL413: Yes · 0 No · 0\nL414: \nL415: [Button: Report ]\nL416: \nL417:   2. Anonymous\nL418: \nL419: · a year ago\nL420: ### How can I determine the shelf life / expiration / retest date of this product?\nL421: \nL422: 1 answer\nL423: \nL424:     1. Technical Support\nL425: \nL426: · a year ago\nL427: If this product has an expiration or retest date, it will be shown on the Certificate of Analysis (COA, CofA). If there is no retest or expiration date listed on the product's COA, we do not have suitable stability data to determine a shelf life. For these products, the only date on the COA will be the release date; a retest, expiration, or use-by-date will not be displayed.\nL428: For all products, we recommend handling per defined conditions as printed in our product literature and website product descriptions. We recommend that products should be routinely inspected by customers to ensure they perform as expected.\nL429: For products without retest or expiration dates, our standard warranty of 1 year from the date of shipment is applicable.\nL430: For more information, please refer to the Product Dating Information document: 【35†https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/deepweb/assets/sigmaaldrich/marketing/global/documents/418/501/product-dating-information-06-25-mk.pdf】\nL431: Helpful?\nL432: \nL433: Yes · 0 No · 0\nL434: \nL435: [Button: Report ]\nL436: \nL437:   3. Anonymous\nL438: \nL439: · 2 years ago\nL440: ### How is shipping temperature determined? And how is it related to the product storage temperature?\nL441: \nL442: 1 answer\nL443: \nL444:     1. Technical Support\nL445: \nL446: · 2 years ago\nL447: Products may be shipped at a different temperature than the recommended long-term storage temperature. If the product quality is sensitive to short-term exposure to conditions other than the recommended long-term storage, it will be shipped on wet or dry-ice. If the product quality is NOT affected by short-term exposure to conditions other than the recommended long-term storage, it will be shipped at ambient temperature.\nL448: As shipping routes are configured for minimum transit times, shipping at ambient temperature helps control shipping costs for our customers. For more information, please refer to the Storage and Transport Conditions document: 【36†https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/deepweb/assets/sigmaaldrich/marketing/global/documents/316/622/storage-transport-conditions-mk.pdf】\nL449: Helpful?\nL450: \nL451: Yes · 0 No · 0\nL452: \nL453: [Button: Report ]\nL454: \nL455:   4. · 2 years ago\nL456: ### What concentration of HEPES should be used for cell culture without CO2, to maintain optimal pH?\nL457: \nL458: 1 answer\nL459: \nL460:     1. Technical Support\nL461: \nL462: · 2 years ago\nL463: This product has not been tested for cell culture use. A better choice is H4034 HEPES BioPerformance Certified, ?99.5% (titration), suitable for cell culture, or one of the other products referred to in the Technical Bulletin found in the documentation section of the product page:\nL464: 【37†https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/product/sigma/h4034#product-documentation】\nL465: \nL466: Helpful?\nL467: \nL468: Yes · 0 No · 0\nL469: \nL470: [Button: Report ]\nL471: \nL472:   5. Anonymous\nL473: \nL474: · 4 years ago\nL475: \nL476: What is the purpose of using HEPES in cell culture?\nL477: \nL478: 1 answer\nL479:     1. Technical Support\nL480: \nL481: · 4 years ago\nL482: \nL483: HEPES provides supplemental buffering for media in pH range of 7.2 to 7.6. It has no nutritional value to cells.\nL484: \nL485: Helpful?\nL486: \nL487: Yes · 0 No · 0\nL488: \nL489: [Button: Report ]\nL490: \nL491:   6. Anonymous\nL492: \nL493: · 4 years ago\nL494: \nL495: What is the Department of Transportation shipping information for this product?\nL496: \nL497: 1 answer\nL498: \nL499:     1. Technical Support\nL500: \nL501: · 4 years ago\nL502: Transportation information can be found in Section 14 of the product's (M)SDS.To access the shipping information for this material, use the link on the product detail page for the product.\nL503: \nL504: Helpful?\nL505: \nL506: Yes · 0 No · 0\nL507: \nL508: [Button: Report ]\nL509: \nL510:   7. Anonymous\nL511: \nL512: · 4 years ago\nL513: \nL514: What is the concentration of HEPES used in cell culture?\nL515: \nL516: 1 answer\nL517: \nL518:     1. Technical Support\nL519: \nL520: · 4 years ago\nL521: \nL522: HEPES is typically used in cell culture in the range of 10-25 mM.\nL523: \nL524: Helpful?\nL525: \nL526: Yes · 0 No · 1\nL527: \nL528: [Button: Report ]\nL529: ## Reviews\nL530: \nL531: Write a review . This action will open a modal dialog.\nL532: \nL533: ### Rating Snapshot\nL534: \nL535: Select a row below to filter reviews.\nL536: \nL537: 5★ stars\nL538: \nL539: 1 1 review with 5 stars. Select to filter reviews with 5 stars.\nL540: \nL541: 4★ stars\nL542: \nL543: 0 0 reviews with 4 stars. Select to filter reviews with 4 stars.\nL544: \nL545: 3★ stars\nL546: \nL547: 0 0 reviews with 3 stars. Select to filter reviews with 3 stars.\nL548: \nL549: 2★ stars\nL550: \nL551: 0 0 reviews with 2 stars. Select to filter reviews with 2 stars.\nL552: \nL553: 1★ stars\nL554: \nL555: 0 0 reviews with 1 star. Select to filter reviews with 1 star.\nL556: ### Average Custo